{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-32818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/assets/99504eaa41497c5be9baa7c860c97ab5ba5c858609e47ad347f24ec9b8ffc940.png)\n\nFind the parametric equations of the line shown in the figure above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6df8a22ab6613a0ac23a24d7a570dcc89032d4ec2bc04f58861496b28aa9696"} {"question" "q-32818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that the line passes through the points $P(3,6,8)$ and $Q(-2,-5,4).$ Now, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-5t \\\\ -11t \\\\ -4t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3-5t \\\\ 6-11t \\\\ 8-4t\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Therefore, the parametric equations are:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3-5t \\\\ y=6-11t \\\\ z=8-4t\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6df8a22ab6613a0ac23a24d7a570dcc89032d4ec2bc04f58861496b28aa9696"} {"question" "q-32818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0a5fa4c061b9091b559daed5e7cf199e8cbd4424fb2052b10cdc24cbb318621"} {"question" "q-32818" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6df8a22ab6613a0ac23a24d7a570dcc89032d4ec2bc04f58861496b28aa9696"} {"question" "q-32818" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2+3t \\\\ y=-5+6t \\\\ z=4+8t\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x=-5+3t \\\\ y=-11+6t \\\\ z=-4+8t\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x=-5t \\\\ y=-11t \\\\ z=-4t\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x=3-5t \\\\ y=6-11t \\\\ z=8-4t\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x=3t \\\\ y=6t \\\\ z=8t\\end{aligned}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6df8a22ab6613a0ac23a24d7a570dcc89032d4ec2bc04f58861496b28aa9696"} {"question" "q-32818" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}x=3-5t \\\\ y=6-11t \\\\ z=8-4t\\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6df8a22ab6613a0ac23a24d7a570dcc89032d4ec2bc04f58861496b28aa9696"} {"question" "q-36026" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the parametric equations of the line that passes through the points $P(1,4,-2)$ and $Q(5,3,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6df8a22ab6613a0ac23a24d7a570dcc89032d4ec2bc04f58861496b28aa9696"} {"question" "q-36026" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that the line passes through the points $P(1,4,-2)$ and $Q(5,3,0).$ Now, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4t \\\\ -t \\\\ 2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1+4t \\\\ 4-t \\\\ -2+2t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ And finally, the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1+4t \\\\ y=4-t \\\\ z=-2+2t\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6df8a22ab6613a0ac23a24d7a570dcc89032d4ec2bc04f58861496b28aa9696"} {"question" "q-36026" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0a5fa4c061b9091b559daed5e7cf199e8cbd4424fb2052b10cdc24cbb318621"} {"question" "q-36026" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6df8a22ab6613a0ac23a24d7a570dcc89032d4ec2bc04f58861496b28aa9696"} {"question" "q-36026" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x=1+4t \\\\ y=4-t \\\\ z=-2+2t\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x=4+t \\\\ y=-1+4t \\\\ z=2-2t\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x=4t \\\\ y=-t \\\\ z=2t\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x=5+t \\\\ y=3+4t \\\\ z=-2t\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x=t \\\\ y=4t \\\\ z=-2t\\end{aligned}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6df8a22ab6613a0ac23a24d7a570dcc89032d4ec2bc04f58861496b28aa9696"} {"question" "q-36026" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}x=1+4t \\\\ y=4-t \\\\ z=-2+2t\\end{aligned}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6df8a22ab6613a0ac23a24d7a570dcc89032d4ec2bc04f58861496b28aa9696"} {"question" "q-70722" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{1}{2}t+1 \\\\ y=5-\\frac{1}{2}t \\\\ z=2t+\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6df8a22ab6613a0ac23a24d7a570dcc89032d4ec2bc04f58861496b28aa9696"} {"question" "q-70722" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}t+1 \\\\ 5-\\frac{1}{2}t \\\\ 2t+\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}t \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}t \\\\ 2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $(1,5,\\frac{1}{3})$  and is parallel to the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6df8a22ab6613a0ac23a24d7a570dcc89032d4ec2bc04f58861496b28aa9696"} {"question" "q-70722" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0a5fa4c061b9091b559daed5e7cf199e8cbd4424fb2052b10cdc24cbb318621"} {"question" "q-70722" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6df8a22ab6613a0ac23a24d7a570dcc89032d4ec2bc04f58861496b28aa9696"} {"question" "q-70722" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6df8a22ab6613a0ac23a24d7a570dcc89032d4ec2bc04f58861496b28aa9696"} {"question" "q-70722" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6df8a22ab6613a0ac23a24d7a570dcc89032d4ec2bc04f58861496b28aa9696"} {"question" "q-236389" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Fill in the missing parts in the parametric equations below that describe all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(1,4,-2)$ and $Q(-2,3,1).$\n\n| $x=$ | {{field-1}} | $t\\in [0,$ {{field-2}} $]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y=$ | $4-t$ |  |\n| $z=$ | {{field-3}} |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6df8a22ab6613a0ac23a24d7a570dcc89032d4ec2bc04f58861496b28aa9696"} {"question" "q-236389" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the line passing through the given points. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3t \\\\ -t \\\\ 3t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1-3t \\\\ 4-t \\\\ -2+3t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nTo get the equations for the line segment, we take only $t\\in [0,1].$ Notice that substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1-3t \\\\ y=4-t \\\\ z=-2+3t\\end{aligned}\\,\\,t\\in [0,1]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6df8a22ab6613a0ac23a24d7a570dcc89032d4ec2bc04f58861496b28aa9696"} {"question" "q-236389" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0a5fa4c061b9091b559daed5e7cf199e8cbd4424fb2052b10cdc24cbb318621"} {"question" "q-236389" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6df8a22ab6613a0ac23a24d7a570dcc89032d4ec2bc04f58861496b28aa9696"} {"question" "q-236389" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "valu